{"id":"mahabharata-3-259","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":259,"title":"एकोनषष्ट्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 259 · The birth and boons of Ravana","summary":{"en":"Vishravas, born of half of Pulastya's body, is angry with Kubera, and Kubera gives him Rakshasa women who bear Ravana, Kumbhakarna, Vibhishana, Khara and Shurpanakha. By fierce austerities the brothers win boons from Brahma, Ravana immunity from all but men, Vibhishana steadfastness in dharma, Kumbhakarna long sleep; Ravana then drives Kubera out of Lanka.","kn":"ಪುಲಸ್ತ್ಯನ ಅರ್ಧದೇಹದಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ವಿಶ್ರವಸು ಕುಬೇರನ ಮೇಲೆ ಕೋಪಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕುಬೇರನು ಅವನಿಗೆ ರಾಕ್ಷಸಿಯರನ್ನು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವರಿಂದ ರಾವಣ, ಕುಂಭಕರ್ಣ, ವಿಭೀಷಣ, ಖರ, ಶೂರ್ಪಣಖೆಯರು ಹುಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಉಗ್ರತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನಿಂದ ವರ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ: ರಾವಣನಿಗೆ ಮನುಷ್ಯರನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಎಲ್ಲರಿಂದ ಅವಧ್ಯತೆ, ವಿಭೀಷಣನಿಗೆ ಧರ್ಮನಿಷ್ಠೆ, ಕುಂಭಕರ್ಣನಿಗೆ ದೀರ್ಘನಿದ್ರೆ; ಅನಂತರ ರಾವಣನು ಕುಬೇರನನ್ನು ಲಂಕೆಯಿಂದ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पुलस्त्य के आधे शरीर से जन्मे विश्रवा कुबेर पर क्रुद्ध होते हैं, और कुबेर उन्हें राक्षसियाँ देते हैं, जिनसे रावण, कुम्भकर्ण, विभीषण, खर और शूर्पणखा जन्मते हैं। उग्र तप से भाई ब्रह्मा से वर पाते हैं: रावण को मनुष्यों को छोड़ सबसे अवध्यता, विभीषण को धर्म में दृढ़ता, कुम्भकर्ण को दीर्घ निद्रा; फिर रावण कुबेर को लंका से भगा देता है।","te":"పులస్త్యుని అర్ధదేహం నుండి పుట్టిన విశ్రవసుడు కుబేరునిపై కోపిస్తాడు; కుబేరుడు అతనికి రాక్షసస్త్రీలను ఇస్తాడు, వారి నుండి రావణుడు, కుంభకర్ణుడు, విభీషణుడు, ఖరుడు, శూర్పణఖ పుడతారు. ఉగ్రతపస్సుతో బ్రహ్మ నుండి వరాలు పొందుతారు: రావణునికి మనుషులు తప్ప అందరి చేత అవధ్యత్వం, విభీషణునికి ధర్మనిష్ఠ, కుంభకర్ణునికి దీర్ఘనిద్ర; తర్వాత రావణుడు కుబేరుని లంక నుండి తరిమివేస్తాడు.","ta":"புலஸ்த்யரின் பாதி உடலிலிருந்து பிறந்த விஶ்ரவஸ் குபேரன் மீது சினமுற, குபேரன் அவருக்கு அரக்கியரை அளிக்கிறான்; அவர்களிடமிருந்து ராவணன், கும்பகர்ணன், விபீஷணன், கரன், ஶூர்ப்பணகை பிறக்கிறார்கள். கடுந்தவத்தால் ப்ரஹ்மாவிடம் வரம் பெறுகிறார்கள்: ராவணனுக்கு மனிதர் தவிர அனைவராலும் கொல்லப்படாமை, விபீஷணனுக்கு அற உறுதி, கும்பகர்ணனுக்கு நீண்ட உறக்கம்; பின் ராவணன் குபேரனை லங்கையிலிருந்து விரட்டுகிறான்.","ml":"പുലസ്ത്യന്റെ ശരീരത്തിന്റെ പകുതിയിൽനിന്ന് ജനിച്ച വിശ്രവസ്സ് കുബേരനോട് കോപിക്കുന്നു; കുബേരൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് രാക്ഷസസ്ത്രീകളെ നൽകുന്നു, അവരിൽനിന്ന് രാവണൻ, കുംഭകർണ്ണൻ, വിഭീഷണൻ, ഖരൻ, ശൂർപ്പണഖ എന്നിവർ ജനിക്കുന്നു. കഠിന തപസ്സിലൂടെ സഹോദരന്മാർ ബ്രഹ്മാവിൽനിന്ന് വരങ്ങൾ നേടുന്നു: രാവണന് മനുഷ്യനൊഴികെ മറ്റാരാലും മരണമില്ലാത്ത അവസ്ഥ, വിഭീഷണന് ധർമ്മത്തിൽ ഉറപ്പ്, കുംഭകർണ്ണന് ദീർഘനിദ്ര; പിന്നെ രാവണൻ കുബേരനെ ലങ്കയിൽനിന്ന് പുറത്താക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.259; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुलस्त्यस्य तु यः क्रोधादर्धदेहोऽभवन्मुनिः ।\nविश्रवा नाम सक्रोधः स वैश्रवणमैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage who was born as half of Pulastya's body from his anger, named Vishrava, looked at Vaishravana angrily."}},{"n":2,"text":"बुबुधे तं तु सक्रोधं पितरं राक्षसेश्वरः ।\nकुबेरस्तत्प्रसादार्थं यतते स्म सदा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kubera, lord of the rakshasas, realized his father was angry and always strove to win his favor, O king."}},{"n":3,"text":"स राजराजो लङ्कायां निवसन्नरवाहनः ।\nराक्षसीः प्रददौ तिस्रः पितुर्वै परिचारिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living in Lanka, that king of kings, who rides on men, gave three rakshasa women to his father as attendants."}},{"n":4,"text":"तास्तदा तं महात्मानं संतोषयितुमुद्यताः ।\nऋषिं भरतशार्दूल नृत्तगीतविशारदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They, skilled in dance and song, set about pleasing that great sage, tiger among the Bharatas."}},{"n":5,"text":"पुष्पोत्कटा च राका च मालिनी च विशां पते ।\nअन्योन्यस्पर्धया राजञ्श्रेयस्कामाः सुमध्यमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pushpotkata, Raka and Malini, lord of men, slender-waisted and seeking their good, competed with each other."}},{"n":6,"text":"तासां स भगवांस्तुष्टो महात्मा प्रददौ वरान् ।\nलोकपालोपमान्पुत्रानेकैकस्या यथेप्सितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pleased and great-souled revered one gave them boons: sons like the world-guardians for each one, as she wished."}},{"n":7,"text":"पुष्पोत्कटायां जज्ञाते द्वौ पुत्रौ राक्षसेश्वरौ ।\nकुम्भकर्णदशग्रीवौ बलेनाप्रतिमौ भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pushpotkata bore two sons, lords of the rakshasas, Kumbhakarna and Dashagriva, unmatched in strength on earth."}},{"n":8,"text":"मालिनी जनयामास पुत्रमेकं विभीषणम् ।\nराकायां मिथुनं जज्ञे खरः शूर्पणखा तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Malini bore one son, Vibhishana. Raka bore twins, Khara and Shurpanakha."}},{"n":9,"text":"विभीषणस्तु रूपेण सर्वेभ्योऽभ्यधिकोऽभवत् ।\nस बभूव महाभागो धर्मगोप्ता क्रियारतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vibhishana surpassed all in beauty; he was very fortunate, a protector of dharma and devoted to right action."}},{"n":10,"text":"दशग्रीवस्तु सर्वेषां ज्येष्ठो राक्षसपुंगवः ।\nमहोत्साहो महावीर्यो महासत्त्वपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dashagriva was the eldest of all, a bull among rakshasas, of great energy, great valor, and great courage and strength."}},{"n":11,"text":"कुम्भकर्णो बलेनासीत्सर्वेभ्योऽभ्यधिकस्तदा ।\nमायावी रणशौण्डश्च रौद्रश्च रजनीचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kumbhakarna was then greater than all in strength, a master of illusion, bold in battle, fearsome, a night-prowler."}},{"n":12,"text":"खरो धनुषि विक्रान्तो ब्रह्मद्विट्पिशिताशनः ।\nसिद्धविघ्नकरी चापि रौद्रा शूर्पणखा तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Khara was powerful with the bow, an enemy of brahmins and a flesh-eater; and fierce Shurpanakha troubled the rites of the perfected."}},{"n":13,"text":"सर्वे वेदविदः शूराः सर्वे सुचरितव्रताः ।\nऊषुः पित्रा सह रता गन्धमादनपर्वते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All were knowers of the Vedas, brave and of fine vows, and lived with their father in contentment on Mount Gandhamadana."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो वैश्रवणं तत्र ददृशुर्नरवाहनम् ।\nपित्रा सार्धं समासीनमृद्ध्या परमया युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they saw Vaishravana, who rides on men, seated with his father in great prosperity."}},{"n":15,"text":"जातस्पर्धास्ततस्ते तु तपसे धृतनिश्चयाः ।\nब्रह्माणं तोषयामासुर्घोरेण तपसा तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filled with rivalry, they resolved on austerity and pleased Brahma with terrible austerity."}},{"n":16,"text":"अतिष्ठदेकपादेन सहस्रं परिवत्सरान् ।\nवायुभक्षो दशग्रीवः पञ्चाग्निः सुसमाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a thousand years Dashagriva stood on one foot, living on air, between five fires, deeply concentrated."}},{"n":17,"text":"अधःशायी कुम्भकर्णो यताहारो यतव्रतः ।\nविभीषणः शीर्णपर्णमेकमभ्यवहारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kumbhakarna lay on the bare ground, restrained in food and vows. Vibhishana ate a single fallen leaf."}},{"n":18,"text":"उपवासरतिर्धीमान्सदा जप्यपरायणः ।\nतमेव कालमातिष्ठत्तीव्रं तप उदारधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He, wise and always devoted to muttered prayers, delighted in fasting, and the noble-minded one practiced fierce austerity for that same time."}},{"n":19,"text":"खरः शूर्पणखा चैव तेषां वै तप्यतां तपः ।\nपरिचर्यां च रक्षां च चक्रतुर्हृष्टमानसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Khara and Shurpanakha, glad in mind, served and guarded them while they performed their austerity."}},{"n":20,"text":"पूर्णे वर्षसहस्रे तु शिरश्छित्त्वा दशाननः ।\nजुहोत्यग्नौ दुराधर्षस्तेनातुष्यज्जगत्प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a thousand years were complete, the unassailable Dashanana cut off his head and offered it into the fire, and the lord of the world was pleased by that."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो ब्रह्मा स्वयं गत्वा तपसस्तान्न्यवारयत् ।\nप्रलोभ्य वरदानेन सर्वानेव पृथक्पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brahma himself went and stopped them from further austerity, tempting each separately with a boon."}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रीतोऽस्मि वो निवर्तध्वं वरान्वृणुत पुत्रकाः ।\nयद्यदिष्टमृते त्वेकममरत्वं तथास्तु तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am pleased with you; turn back, my children, and choose boons. Whatever you want, except immortality, let it be so."}},{"n":23,"text":"यद्यदग्नौ हुतं सर्वं शिरस्ते महदीप्सया ।\nतथैव तानि ते देहे भविष्यन्ति यथेप्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever head of yours was offered into the fire from your great desire, those heads will be as they were on your body, as you wish."}},{"n":24,"text":"वैरूप्यं च न ते देहे कामरूपधरस्तथा ।\nभविष्यसि रणेऽरीणां विजेतासि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There will be no deformity in your body and you will take any form at will. You will be victorious over your enemies in battle, without doubt."}},{"text":"रावण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ravana said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"गन्धर्वदेवासुरतो यक्षराक्षसतस्तथा ।\nसर्पकिंनरभूतेभ्यो न मे भूयात्पराभवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let me never be defeated by gandharvas, gods, asuras, yakshas, rakshasas, serpents, kinnaras or spirits."}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"य एते कीर्तिताः सर्वे न तेभ्योऽस्ति भयं तव ।\nऋते मनुष्याद्भद्रं ते तथा तद्विहितं मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have no fear from any of those you have named, except from a man. Good luck to you; so I have arranged it."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"एवमुक्तो दशग्रीवस्तुष्टः समभवत्तदा ।\nअवमेने हि दुर्बुद्धिर्मनुष्यान्पुरुषादकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Dashagriva was pleased. The evil-minded man-eater despised humans."}},{"n":28,"text":"कुम्भकर्णमथोवाच तथैव प्रपितामहः ।\nस वव्रे महतीं निद्रां तमसा ग्रस्तचेतनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-grandfather then spoke likewise to Kumbhakarna, who, with his mind swallowed by darkness, chose a great sleep."}},{"n":29,"text":"तथा भविष्यतीत्युक्त्वा विभीषणमुवाच ह ।\nवरं वृणीष्व पुत्र त्वं प्रीतोऽस्मीति पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So it shall be,\" he said to Vibhishana again and again, \"Choose a boon, son; I am pleased.\""}},{"text":"विभीषण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vibhishana said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"परमापद्गतस्यापि नाधर्मे मे मतिर्भवेत् ।\nअशिक्षितं च भगवन्ब्रह्मास्त्रं प्रतिभातु मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if I were in extreme distress, may my mind not turn to adharma. And, revered one, let the Brahma weapon, which I have not been taught, come to me."}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"यस्माद्राक्षसयोनौ ते जातस्यामित्रकर्शन ।\nनाधर्मे रमते बुद्धिरमरत्वं ददामि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since, though born in a rakshasa womb, your mind does not delight in adharma, scorcher of foes, I give you immortality."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"राक्षसस्तु वरं लब्ध्वा दशग्रीवो विशां पते ।\nलङ्कायाश्च्यावयामास युधि जित्वा धनेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasa Dashagriva, having gained his boon, lord of men, defeated the lord of wealth in battle and drove him from Lanka."}},{"n":33,"text":"हित्वा स भगवाँल्लङ्कामाविशद्गन्धमादनम् ।\nगन्धर्वयक्षानुगतो रक्षःकिंपुरुषैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up Lanka, the revered one went to Gandhamadana, followed by gandharvas and yakshas, with rakshasas and kimpurushas."}},{"n":34,"text":"विमानं पुष्पकं तस्य जहाराक्रम्य रावणः ।\nशशाप तं वैश्रवणो न त्वामेतद्वहिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ravana attacked and seized his chariot Pushpaka. Vaishravana cursed him: \"This will not carry you."}},{"n":35,"text":"यस्तु त्वां समरे हन्ता तमेवैतद्वहिष्यति ।\nअवमन्य गुरुं मां च क्षिप्रं त्वं न भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"It will carry only the one who kills you in battle. Having scorned me, your elder, you will soon be no more.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"विभीषणस्तु धर्मात्मा सतां धर्ममनुस्मरन् ।\nअन्वगच्छन्महाराज श्रिया परमया युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Vibhishana, righteous, remembering the dharma of the good, followed him, great king, endowed with great splendor."}},{"n":37,"text":"तस्मै स भगवांस्तुष्टो भ्राता भ्रात्रे धनेश्वरः ।\nसेनापत्यं ददौ धीमान्यक्षराक्षससेनयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The revered lord of wealth, pleased with his brother, wise, gave him command of the armies of yakshas and rakshasas."}},{"n":38,"text":"राक्षसाः पुरुषादाश्च पिशाचाश्च महाबलाः ।\nसर्वे समेत्य राजानमभ्यषिञ्चद्दशाननम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasas, man-eaters and mighty pishachas all came together and consecrated Dashanana as king."}},{"n":39,"text":"दशग्रीवस्तु दैत्यानां देवानां च बलोत्कटः ।\nआक्रम्य रत्नान्यहरत्कामरूपी विहंगमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dashagriva, strong, attacked the Daityas and the gods and carried off their jewels, flying about as he pleased."}},{"n":40,"text":"रावयामास लोकान्यत्तस्माद्रावण उच्यते ।\nदशग्रीवः कामबलो देवानां भयमादधत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because he made the worlds cry out, he is called Ravana. Dashagriva, strong at will, brought fear on the gods."}}]}]}